  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Uganda Civic Space Case Study</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Civic Space Case Study project is  a learning project of the Knowledge Hub to document  needs, desires, questions, doubts, ideas, with the purpose of facilitating conversations and building consensus around issues of Civic Space in Uganda. This project is to aide thinking through the process that is most useful in country, to drive the country process in a context specific manner, and to jointly contribute to the overarching approach. This project takes on the methodology of small group discussions, focus group discussions and one on one interviews, through targeting different stakeholders like justice actors, media and CSOs.

Oxfam in Uganda willidentify and map out the participants, who will respond in the small group discussions, focus group discussions and one on one interviews. Oxfam will also compile FGD transcripts, summaries of key discussion points, and recommendations. Oxfam will also prepare interview questions and compile interview report and with small group discussions, Oxfam will carry out the selection of participants,and will guide documentation of discussion summaries, highlighting emerging themes and and personal reflections.</narrative>
  </description>
